{"type":"message","id":"3d96e64d","parentId":"22159d2d","timestamp":"2026-03-25T06:35:54.459Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conclusion:**\n\nUnfortunately, InfinBiz uses a single-page application (SPA) architecture. The inventory system doesn't have a dedicated URL for adding items — it's all handled via client-side JavaScript modals.\n\n**What I found:**\n- `/inventory/new` — returns a blank page\n- `/inventory/add` — 404 error\n- `/products` — 404 error\n- `/product-catalog` — not found\n\n**The limitation:** When I try to run JavaScript that simulates clicks or dispatches events, the browser tab disconnects. This is a constraint of the current browser automation tool.\n\n**What works:**\n- Navigating to pages\n- Taking snapshots/screenshots\n- Running simple JavaScript queries\n- `navigate` with `javaScript` parameter (for simple scripts)\n\n**What doesn't work:**\n- Complex event simulation (causes disconnects)\n- The `actions` API (rejected by the tool)\n\n**For your use case:** The \"Add Item\" button requires clicking it manually in the browser. Once clicked, the modal should appear and you can enter item details directly.\n\nWant me to document this for future reference, or would you like to try a different approach?"}],"stopReason":"stop","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"kimi-k2.5:cloud","usage":{"input":35035,"output":298,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":35333,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1774420554458}}
