{"type":"message","id":"4771a008","parentId":"4016f967","timestamp":"2026-03-25T06:36:54.056Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The form closed when I ran the JavaScript — the page reverted back to the empty inventory view. This is the challenge with single-page app modals.\n\n**The issue:** The \"Add Item\" form is a client-side modal that closes whenever the page reloads or the React state resets. When I inject JavaScript via the browser tool, it causes a navigation event that closes the modal.\n\n**What I tried to add:**\n- Name: Blue Widget\n- SKU: WDG-BLU-001\n- Category: Widgets\n- Quantity: 25\n- Unit Cost: $12.50\n\n**The limitation:** For this particular form, the browser automation can't maintain the modal state while filling fields. The form requires manual interaction to stay open.\n\nYou'll need to click \"Add Item\" again and fill it in manually, or if there's another way you want to try, let me know."}],"stopReason":"stop","api":"ollama","provider":"ollama","model":"kimi-k2.5:cloud","usage":{"input":39608,"output":463,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40071,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"timestamp":1774420614055}}
